1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,066
Imagine you have $3.67 million in only three months to spend in Virginia.

2
00:00:06,066 --> 00:00:09,300
You could pay the salary for 212 teachers,

3
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:12,500
cover the monthly energy bills for 6,700 households,

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,433
or fund school lunches for close to 60,000 kids.

5
00:00:15,433 --> 00:00:18,100
Dominion Energy had that $3.67 million,

6
00:00:18,166 --> 00:00:20,833
and it spent every last penny on political contributions,

7
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:22,900
and all of that just within the last three months,

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:27,000
when Virginia has been weighing whether to approve a $67 billion proposal

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,233
that would create the world's largest regulated electric utility.

10
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:33,966
The timing of Dominion's unprecedented off-year spending should have everyone wondering

11
00:00:33,966 --> 00:00:36,766
who actually has the power to influence the outcome of that decision.

12
00:00:36,766 --> 00:00:39,366
If Dominion gets its way and NextEra takes over,

13
00:00:39,366 --> 00:00:43,266
the company doing the spending will get even bigger, and so will the risk of political corruption.

14
00:00:43,266 --> 00:00:47,300
Virginians deserve to know who will stand up for them when the stakes are this high.

15
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,966
If you're worried about this deal like Teddy is, your lawmakers need to hear from you.

16
00:00:50,966 --> 00:00:53,300
Contact them today and share your concerns.

17
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:55,533
Ask them what they're doing to protect their constituents,

18
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,466
and urge them to come out publicly in opposition to the acquisition

19
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,166
and in support of Virginia families.
